## Finding, measured (host npm --version = 12.2.2, node v22.22.3, better-sqlite3 12.11.1)
1. Reproduction: a scratch install with no allowScripts exits 0 and warns
   "1 package had install scripts blocked because they are not covered by allowScripts:
    better-sqlite3@12.11.1 (install: prebuild-install || node-gyp rebuild --release)";
   require('better-sqlite3') then fails with "Could not locate the bindings file".
2. `npm install-scripts approve --no-allow-scripts-pin better-sqlite3` exits 0, prints
   "Approved better-sqlite3: / added better-sqlite3" and writes the unpinned allowScripts entry.
   It builds NOTHING — the binding is still missing immediately after it.
3. `npm rebuild better-sqlite3` exits 0, creates build/Release/better_sqlite3.node, and
   require + select sqlite_version() -> 3.53.2 succeeds; the repo gate prints
   "OK: better-sqlite3 native binding loads (SELECT 1 -> {"x":1})".

=> The printed remedy is CORRECT as printed; no remedy command was changed. Two measured traps were
   added to the script text and the README: (a) `npm rebuild` exits 0 while the install script is still
   blocked, so judge the fix by `npm run check:sqlite-binding`, never by rebuild's exit code;
   (b) an explicit `"better-sqlite3": false` deny entry makes `approve` a green no-op that has to be
   deleted by hand.

